2026-05-27 14:23:13,811 | AGENT | Final proposal generated: # Executive Summary
The consortium led by Nexus Engineering S.r.l., in collaboration with LexIA GmbH and EuroCloud Solutions S.A., proposes a comprehensive artificial intelligence solution to assist the City of Belval's municipal agents in their daily tasks. Our proposal leverages large language models (LLMs), retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) capabilities, and expertise in GDPR compliance, AI security controls, and sovereign cloud hosting to provide an efficient and secure assistance tool. With a strong focus on innovation, sustainability, and regulatory adherence, we aim to enhance the quality of service rendered to users while reducing processing times.

# Understanding of Requirements
The City of Belval seeks to implement an artificial intelligence solution that assists municipal agents in accessing information, drafting administrative contents, instructing files, and suggesting actions or steps within administrative processes. The solution must integrate with existing systems, ensure data protection and GDPR compliance, provide explicability and transparency, and meet specific performance and availability requirements.

# Proposed Solution
Our proposed solution involves deploying a sovereign LLM like Mistral 7B Instruct, fine-tuned using LoRA or QLoRA methods to adapt to the administrative tone and format required by the City of Belval. We will utilize RAG capabilities with semantic chunking and hybrid retrieval strategies for accurate information search and suggestion of actions within administrative processes. The solution will be hosted on SecNumCloud-certified infrastructure within the EU, using providers like Outscale or OVHcloud, ensuring no dependency on non-European suppliers.

For API integration, we will use standards like REST, GraphQL, or SOAP, and API gateways like Kong or Apigee to integrate with civil-status and town-planning software, EDM systems like Alfresco or Maarch Courrier, and user directories using protocols like SAML 2.0 or OpenID Connect. To achieve 99.9% availability, we will design a highly available architecture using containerization with Docker and Kubernetes, and monitoring tools like Prometheus and Grafana.

Our solution will ensure GDPR compliance through strict data residency set to EU only, cross-border transfer policy prohibited by default, and utilization of anonymisation tools like Microsoft Presidio and custom NER models. AI security controls will include prompt injection protection, output PII redaction, adversarial input detection, confidence threshold escalation, and model isolation.

We project a margin of 840,000 euros based on a hypothetical project budget of 3 million euros over 4 years, using our standard pricing model and target gross margin percentage of 28. For cost optimization, we can absorb a 10% budget reduction via rate renegotiation with subcontractors.

To reduce the environmental footprint, we will leverage green hosting providers OVHcloud and Scaleway, who use 100% renewable energy and have a low Power Usage Effectiveness (PUE) of 1.3 and 1.28 respectively. Our digital sobriety practices, including INT8/INT4 model quantisation, auto-scaling to zero outside business hours, query result caching, and green IT hardware procurement policy, can lead to an estimated 35% reduction in energy consumption.

# Unaddressed Requirements
None of the requirements from the tender are left unaddressed by our proposal. However, we note that the Budget Agent did not have specific information about a project with a global budget allocated of 3 million euros over 4 years but provided hypothetical calculations based on standard pricing models.

# Conclusion
Our consortium offers a comprehensive and innovative solution that addresses the City of Belval's needs for an artificial intelligence assistance tool. With a strong focus on regulatory compliance, security, sustainability, and performance, we are confident that our proposal meets all the requirements outlined in the tender. We look forward to the opportunity to discuss our proposal in further detail and explore how we can assist the City of Belval in achieving its digital transformation objectives.
